From: Luisyr <106528106+luisyr1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 18:10:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/11] drm/google: gs-decon: hold komodo's boot framebuffer
 aperture

With hold_boot_fb, variant B (gs_decon.stage=2) can keep the
simple-framebuffer node as a fallback: if gs-decon takes the display,
simpledrm cannot register a second output on the same buffer; if gs-decon
does not (stage 1, failed probe), simpledrm keeps the console. Stage 1 is
unchanged (the hold is only taken on the KMS path). Same setting raven
(gs101) runs with.

Not tested on hardware.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/google/gs-decon.c | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/google/gs-decon.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/google/gs-decon.c
index c36c81747..3205fb68d 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/google/gs-decon.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/google/gs-decon.c
@@ -330,7 +330,13 @@ static const struct gs_decon_soc_data zumapro_decon_data = {
 	.floors_optional = true,
 };
 
-/* Komodo's bootloader handoff was measured on-device at 1344x2992. */
+/*
+ * Komodo's bootloader handoff was measured on-device at 1344x2992. The DT
+ * keeps a simple-framebuffer on the same buffer as a fallback for when
+ * gs-decon does not take the display (stage 1, a failed probe): hold its
+ * aperture after evicting simpledrm, as on raven, so that a simpledrm
+ * probing later does not register a second, phantom output.
+ */
 static const struct gs_decon_soc_data komodo_decon_data = {
 	.modes = komodo_decon_modes,
 	.num_modes = ARRAY_SIZE(komodo_decon_modes),
@@ -341,6 +347,7 @@ static const struct gs_decon_soc_data komodo_decon_data = {
 	.padded_pitch = true,
 	.start_hw_trigger = true,
 	.floors_optional = true,
+	.hold_boot_fb = true,
 };
 
 /* G3 shares G4's CAL (cal_9865) and DECON0 registers. */
